WEBVTT

00:41:29.333 --> 00:41:32.226
and decided that anytime
I have a relationship with someone,

00:41:32.250 --> 00:41:34.934
of course they will know
that when I'm challenging them,

00:41:34.958 --> 00:41:36.601
it's because I want to help them.

00:41:36.625 --> 00:41:40.601
And I've discovered of late that there are
moments when I have not made that clear,

00:41:40.625 --> 00:41:41.893
and I've regretted that.

00:41:41.917 --> 00:41:44.809
EP: What could you have said differently
or done differently?

00:41:44.833 --> 00:41:46.976
AG: I think it's
a simple thing to start out.

00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:50.726
It's fundamentally about just establishing
that tough love is the way you help.

00:41:50.750 --> 00:41:52.059
So what I would have done,

00:41:52.083 --> 00:41:55.434
I think about a situation I had recently
with a student I was advising.

00:41:55.458 --> 00:41:57.934
One of the first things
I could have done is to say,

00:41:57.958 --> 00:41:59.601
"Look, when I was in grad school,

00:41:59.625 --> 00:42:01.893
one of the best things
that a mentor did for me